      "transcript_text": "That's all I needed to check. Putting it all together, this looks most like alcohol withdrawal. Let's get blood tests, for alcohol withdrawal. I'll start you on chlordiazepoxide, 20 milligrams, four times a day, reducing over five days. You take it by mouth. That should help with alcohol withdrawal. What I'm giving you is thiamine, 100 milligrams, three times a day, long term. You take it by mouth. That should help with alcohol-related deficiency.",
